Description: A simple and unified evaluation toolkit for benchmarking single-cell
    and multiomics data simulation methods. Evaluates how realistic simulated data
    are compared to real biological datasets across three multiomics experimental
    designs: (i) paired multiomics (simultaneous co-assay from identical cells,
    e.g. 10x Chromium Multiome, SHARE-seq, SNARE-seq), which unlocks the full
    Category 7 cross-modal coupling suite including FOSCTTM alignment scores and
    peak-to-gene regulatory linkage; (ii) unpaired multiomics (independent scRNA-seq
    and scATAC-seq profiled from separate cells of the same tissue), supported
    through per-modality unimodal evaluation (Categories 1-6, 8) and population-level
    cross-modal metrics such as co-expression module fidelity and network Jaccard
    similarity; and (iii) mosaic multiomics (partial co-measurement where only a
    subset of cells has both modalities, e.g. DOGMA-seq or mosaic pooling designs),
    handled by subsetting the paired cell fraction for coupling metrics and evaluating
    each modality independently otherwise. The toolkit quantifies simulation realism
    using 55 evaluation measures organized into 8 canonical categories:
    (1) Distributional Properties: 10 univariate metrics (Wasserstein, KS, MAD, MAE, RMSE, Bhattacharyya, KDE-ISE, Runs statistic, NN mismatch, Inter-dataset silhouette) and 4 bivariate metrics (Fasano-Franceschini 2D KS, 2D EMD, 2D NN mismatch, 2D Inter-dataset silhouette) evaluated across 7 cell-level, 7 feature-level, and 4 bivariate property pairs,
    (2) Sparsity & Zero-Inflation Dynamics: logistic dropout curve midpoint/slope/R2 (scRNA-seq), quadratic accessibility-sparsity curve RMSE/R2 (scATAC-seq), and posterior excess zero weight discrepancy,
    (3) Cellular Manifold & Clustering Concordance: MMD, Generative Precision/Recall, Silhouette ASW, Clustering Deviation Index (CDI), Neighborhood Purity, ARI, and NMI (with auxiliary Davies-Bouldin Index),
    (4) Technical Variation & Batch Mixing Dynamics: Batch Silhouette, PCR R2, CMS, Inverse Simpson Index (ISI), and Cross-Batch F1,
    (5) Biological Signal & Differential Fidelity: pseudobulk edgeR-QLF null P-value uniformity, accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and ROC-AUC across parallel scRNA-seq DE and scATAC-seq DA sub-categories,
    (6) Multiomics Integration & Alignment: joint-embedding Batch ASW, Cell-Type ASW, Graph Connectivity, Integration ARI, and Integration NMI,
    (7) Trajectory & Lineage Topology: pseudotime correlation, lineage tree RMSE, trajectory graph alignment, and lineage gene expression fidelity,
    (8) Computational Scalability & Efficiency: elapsed runtime (seconds) and peak RAM allocation (MiB).
    Includes non-linear low-dimensional cell embedding projections (UMAP, t-SNE, PCA) with quantitative cluster separability (Silhouette) and fidelity (ARI) metrics, automated score normalization, leaderboards, 600 DPI bubble plots, and an interactive Shiny app studio.
